    "['multi-topology', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'family inet6 {', 'parent_command': ['set protocols bgp local-as [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set protocols bgp local-as [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nfamily inet6 {\\n    topology inet6;\\n}\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, the `multi-topology` command from Cisco IS-IS IPv6 address family configuration is translated to explicitly specify IPv6 topology support under the family inet6 hierarchy.\\n- The `topology inet6` statement enables multi-topology routing for IPv6 in IS-IS, which is the Juniper equivalent of Cisco's `multi-topology` command.\\n- The curly braces and hierarchical structure are Juniper's standard configuration style.\", 'trans_template': 'family inet6 {'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'topology inet6;', 'parent_command': ['set protocols bgp local-as [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set protocols bgp local-as [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nfamily inet6 {\\n    topology inet6;\\n}\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, the `multi-topology` command from Cisco IS-IS IPv6 address family configuration is translated to explicitly specify IPv6 topology support under the family inet6 hierarchy.\\n- The `topology inet6` statement enables multi-topology routing for IPv6 in IS-IS, which is the Juniper equivalent of Cisco's `multi-topology` command.\\n- The curly braces and hierarchical structure are Juniper's standard configuration style.\", 'trans_template': 'topology inet6;'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': '}', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'interfaces { [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nfamily inet6 {\\n    topology inet6;\\n}\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, the `multi-topology` command from Cisco IS-IS IPv6 address family configuration is translated to explicitly specify IPv6 topology support under the family inet6 hierarchy.\\n- The `topology inet6` statement enables multi-topology routing for IPv6 in IS-IS, which is the Juniper equivalent of Cisco's `multi-topology` command.\\n- The curly braces and hierarchical structure are Juniper's standard configuration style.\", 'trans_template': '}'}]]": 1,
